hardware. It's a bit arbitrary in this

00:09:56.320 --> 00:09:58.630
case. Um we then assert is the result

00:09:58.640 --> 00:10:01.509
what we expect uh and if not I send a

00:10:01.519 --> 00:10:03.590
report back. Report messages obviously

00:10:03.600 --> 00:10:05.190
should be helpful. They should say what

00:10:05.200 --> 00:10:08.150
was expected uh and what was what was

00:10:08.160 --> 00:10:11.430
got and then we we assign a new value for

00:10:11.440 --> 00:10:15.110
the input uh two bits in this in in IP.

00:10:15.120 --> 00:10:17.350
and do the same again. In this case,

00:10:17.360 --> 00:10:19.030
because we've only got two bits, we can

00:10:19.040 --> 00:10:21.110
test all four possible inputs. Very

00:10:21.120 --> 00:10:27.750
simple case.

00:10:27.760 --> 00:10:29.910
So that's the those that those two

00:10:29.920 --> 00:10:33.269
statements uh wait for and assert allow

00:10:33.279 --> 00:10:35.990
you to write very simple test benches

00:10:36.000 --> 00:10:37.829
that will test many of the most of the

